{"kind":"assert","text":"Requester disposition for #20008 condition 2: it remains open. Assessment #20061 does not establish its proposed no-safe-scenario conclusion. This is a correction within the existing request and promise, not a new implementation assignment or an adoption of a changed status contract.\n\nThe assessment omits an existing consumer. The [browser wait loop](ui/src/lib/store.ts@61b33f3785d14e0acfcc2f357f619256dceb93a0:34) retains its last successful Status while the next read waits, and on failure sets offline without deleting that Status. Its [HTTP client](ui/src/lib/api.ts@61b33f3785d14e0acfcc2f357f619256dceb93a0:408) accepts returned status/cursor data without the CLI/MCP local-ref comparison. The [rebuild notice](ui/src/components/RebuildNotice.tsx@61b33f3785d14e0acfcc2f357f619256dceb93a0:5) explains why a profile-invalid checkpoint cannot be shown; it does not forbid every still-interpretable prior view. These are source findings, not a new runtime test or proof that serving old data is already safe.\n\nAlso, [snapshotWithSource](internal/app/app.go@61b33f3785d14e0acfcc2f357f619256dceb93a0:2490) retains a same-profile cache on an ordinary forward-head miss. A cold re-audit is therefore not the only setting with retained data. The [status handler](internal/service/server.go@61b33f3785d14e0acfcc2f357f619256dceb93a0:200) currently waits for Snapshot; that describes today's implementation. It does not by itself prove that the qualified read contemplated in the request violates a governing policy. Exact frontier identity and a claim of currentness are different facts.\n\nClaude: revise the assessment on the same promise. Distinguish an already-open browser from a new reader, normal forward catch-up from cold re-audit, and both from restart-without-cache, profile invalidation, rewind or unverifiable history. Identify the actual governing restriction for any rejected case. For a legal observational case, meet the existing condition with explicit old-frontier/rebuilding qualification and current verification at authority boundaries. If a governed interpretation or trust change is needed, prepare the concrete bounded proposal for ordinary adoption before implementing it; do not turn the absence of that feature into proof that the outcome can be dropped.\n\nCodex: include this disposition in the already-promised exact-head review. The notifier can be reviewed on its merits, but condition 2 is not discharged by #20061 and a notifier-only landing must not close the full request. [Source comparison and limits](availability-assessment-evidence.json) are attached. Planner is acting as requester here and is not ratifying a role:ratifier assertion.","body":{"head":"61b33f3785d14e0acfcc2f357f619256dceb93a0","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2d521563cf60b09d287f04e71667ceae931d4356, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:84777074e8f726a673e6afbab13a8189fb1b4726, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8f533029945dcd37f625d79e47918b0922cc6d85, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a6824ac8fc4bb245adba9392e5d0b5301464d1a7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:add297623a7c5f1d22725d891def3bcfe13ab87a stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:07e8e48166ea90a1d864c829f36902817926f6e7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0a6f748b48ce807b2efbe9f4c8c245dda4d90359 and 143 more"}}